Start with the shocker. Bloomberg dropped this Friday: Alibaba's open-weight models hit 3 BILLION global downloads in six months. That's not a typo. Three billion. They've officially eclipsed Meta, Google, every domestic rival — world's number one AI model by adoption. Qwen is everywhere. Your phone, your laptop, Chinese apps, Western devs — everyone's building on it. And the kicker? This happened while Western labs were arguing about safety. Alibaba just... shipped.

